Part I: Road to Initial Production Readiness
Phase 1: Feature Completion and Architectural Alignment
Goal: Finalize core functionality while enforcing absolute compliance with the Architecture Contract's layered security model.
Step 1.0: SignalGateDatabase Companion Object Removal
Fix this before touching anything else. The companion object's getInstance()/buildDatabase()/closeDatabase() methods construct an unencrypted Room database at 'signalgate_multiport.db'. SecureDatabase constructs the encrypted database at 'secure_signal.db'. These are two separate files. Any future code path that calls getInstance() will get a silent, empty, unencrypted database — appearing to the user as all data lost.

Remove getInstance(), buildDatabase(), and closeDatabase() from SignalGateDatabase.kt companion object entirely.
The only permitted construction path is Koin injecting SecureDatabase.getDatabase(androidContext()).
After removal, the companion object itself can be deleted — it has no remaining purpose.
Verify: grep the entire codebase for 'SignalGateDatabase.getInstance' — must return zero results after the fix.
Deliverable: SignalGateDatabase.kt with companion object removed. Zero getInstance() references in codebase.

Step 1.1: First-Install Source Seeding
Prerequisite for Steps 1.2 and 1.3. UnifiedEntryEntity.sourceId is non-nullable with a foreign key constraint. Block/allow inserts will fail without a valid sourceId.

At first database open, check whether each required source row already exists before inserting.
MANUAL source: name = 'Manual User Rules', type = 'MANUAL', pathOrUrl = 'local', isEnabled = true, priority = 100. Used by BlocklistRepository for all user-created block/allow rules.
Contacts Allow List source: name = 'Contacts Allow List', type = 'MANUAL', pathOrUrl = 'contacts', isEnabled = true, priority = 100. Used by ContactsViewModel for all contact imports.
Store both sourceIds in SettingEntry for retrieval without re-querying on every operation.
Logic: query by name first — if row exists, reuse its id. If not, insert and store the new id. Never blindly insert.
Deliverable: DatabaseInitializer (or equivalent) that seeds both source rows idempotently at first install.

Step 1.2: BlocklistRepository.kt
